# ThreadSanitizer suppressions, loaded by run.sh
#
# DiningPhilosophersSemaphore takes the left fork, then the right, so its five
# forks form a lock-order cycle. The semaphore lets at most four philosophers in
# at once, which is what keeps it deadlock-free, but the lock-order checker can't
# see that. A real deadlock would still stop the test from completing.
deadlock:DiningPhilosophersSemaphore::wants_to_eat
